<Positioned left="72" top="1230"><Container width="1096" height="2" color="#241E17FF"/></Positioned>
<Positioned left="72" top="1260"><Text fontSize="15" color="#6B6152FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans Mono CJK SC" fontStyle="BOLD" letterSpacing="2">BAKER'S NOTES</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="72" top="1290"><Text fontSize="17" color="#6B6152FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">Dough entering the retarder at 4 °C is ready to bake between 06:00 and 09:00. If the room climbs above 24 °C, cut bulk</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="72" top="1316"><Text fontSize="17" color="#6B6152FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL"> by 25 minutes rather than chilling the dough — cold shock costs oven spring.</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="72" top="1342"><Text fontSize="17" color="#6B6152FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">Score bâtards at 30° with a single cut. Steam for the first 12 minutes, then vent. Tin loaves go in 20 minutes after the d</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="72" top="1368"><Text fontSize="17" color="#6B6152FF" fontFamily="Noto Sans CJK SC" fontStyle="NORMAL">eck batch.</Text></Positioned>
<Positioned left="0" top="1658"><Container width="1240" height="96" color="#F1EAD9FF"/></Positioned>
